    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it doesn't really feel like something a professional can just \"fix\" though. it's not just being sad, it's that the version of me that they all knew is just... gone. there's no way to go back to how things were before everything went south. it feels like the door is permanently locked and i'm just stuck on the outside looking in forever.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's completely understandable that you feel like this is beyond a simple fix; this feeling of a fundamental self being lost is deeply unsettling. While no one can instantly rewind time, therapy can offer a space to explore *why* that version of you is gone and how to build a new sense of self. Even if you can't go back, there are ways to find connection and meaning in the person you are right now.",
      "source": "target",
